<!-- QUESTION 1 -->

<div class="question">

<div class="question-title">
Question 1 : Online Symposium Portal
</div>

<div class="content">

<h3 class="sub-heading">Given HTML Structure</h3>

<div class="code-box">

&lt;form action="/register" method="POST"&gt;<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;input type="text" name="name"&gt;<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;input type="email" name="email"&gt;<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;button&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;<br>
&lt;/form&gt;

</div>


<div class="answer">

<h3>Answers</h3>

<ol>

<li>
<strong>Missing Semantic Elements :</strong><br>
Header, Main, Section, Labels and Footer elements are missing.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Standards-Compliant Structure :</strong>

<div class="code-box">

&lt;header&gt;<br>
&lt;h1&gt;Symposium Registration&lt;/h1&gt;<br>
&lt;/header&gt;<br><br>

&lt;main&gt;<br>
&lt;section&gt;<br>
&lt;form action="/register" method="POST"&gt;<br>
&lt;label&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt;<br>
&lt;input type="text" required&gt;<br><br>

&lt;label&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt;<br>
&lt;input type="email" required&gt;<br><br>

&lt;button type="submit"&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;<br>
&lt;/form&gt;<br>
&lt;/section&gt;<br>
&lt;/main&gt;

</div>

</li>

<li>
<strong>HTTP Request Interpretation :</strong><br>
The browser sends an HTTP POST request containing the user's information to the server.
</li>

<li>
<strong>HTTP Response Cycle :</strong><br>
Browser → Server receives data → Processes request → Sends response → Browser displays the output.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Usability and Accessibility Improvements :</strong>

<ul>
<li>Use semantic HTML5 elements.</li>
<li>Add labels and required attributes.</li>
<li>Provide validation messages.</li>
<li>Improve keyboard accessibility.</li>
<li>Maintain proper form structure.</li>
</ul>

</li>

</ol>

</div>

</div>
</div>




<!-- QUESTION 2 -->

<div class="question">

<div class="question-title">
Question 2 : Cross-Browser Compatibility Issue
</div>

<div class="content">

<h3 class="sub-heading">Given HTML Structure</h3>

<div class="code-box">

&lt;html&gt;<br>
&lt;head&gt;<br>
&lt;title&gt;Company&lt;/title&gt;<br>
&lt;/head&gt;<br>
&lt;body&gt;<br>
&lt;div&gt;<br>
&lt;h1&gt;Welcome<br>
&lt;p&gt;About us<br>
&lt;/div&gt;<br>
&lt;/body&gt;<br>
&lt;/html&gt;

</div>


<div class="answer">

<h3>Answers</h3>

<ol>

<li>
<strong>Improper Nesting and Missing Tags :</strong><br>
The H1 and P tags are not properly closed.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Browser Interpretation :</strong><br>
Browsers may automatically correct invalid HTML differently, causing inconsistent layouts.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Missing Semantic Elements :</strong><br>
Header, Main and Section elements should be used.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Correct W3C-Compliant HTML Structure :</strong>

<div class="code-box">

&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;<br>
&lt;html&gt;<br>
&lt;head&gt;<br>
&lt;title&gt;Company&lt;/title&gt;<br>
&lt;/head&gt;<br>
&lt;body&gt;<br><br>

&lt;header&gt;<br>
&lt;h1&gt;Welcome&lt;/h1&gt;<br>
&lt;/header&gt;<br><br>

&lt;main&gt;<br>
&lt;section&gt;<br>
&lt;p&gt;About Us&lt;/p&gt;<br>
&lt;/section&gt;<br>
&lt;/main&gt;<br><br>

&lt;/body&gt;<br>
&lt;/html&gt;

</div>

</li>

<li>
<strong>Cross-Browser Compatibility Techniques :</strong>

<ul>
<li>Validate HTML using W3C standards.</li>
<li>Test across multiple browsers.</li>
<li>Use semantic HTML5 tags.</li>
<li>Apply responsive design practices.</li>
<li>Avoid deprecated HTML elements.</li>
</ul>

</li>

</ol>

</div>

</div>
</div>




<!-- QUESTION 3 -->

<div class="question">

<div class="question-title">
Question 3 : Form Submission Failure
</div>

<div class="content">

<h3 class="sub-heading">Given HTML Structure</h3>

<div class="code-box">

&lt;form action="/submit" method="GET"&gt;<br>
&lt;input type="text" name="username"&gt;<br>
&lt;input type="password" name="password"&gt;<br>
&lt;button type="button"&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;<br>
&lt;/form&gt;

</div>


<div class="answer">

<h3>Answers</h3>

<ol>

<li>
<strong>Issues in the Form Configuration :</strong><br>
The form uses the GET method for sensitive information and an incorrect button type.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Why the HTTP Request Is Not Triggered :</strong><br>
The button type is set to "button" instead of "submit."
</li>

<li>
<strong>Role of the GET Method :</strong><br>
GET appends data to the URL and is unsuitable for transmitting passwords.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Correct Implementation :</strong>

<div class="code-box">

&lt;form action="/submit" method="POST"&gt;<br>
&lt;label&gt;Username&lt;/label&gt;<br>
&lt;input type="text" required&gt;<br><br>

&lt;label&gt;Password&lt;/label&gt;<br>
&lt;input type="password" required&gt;<br><br>

&lt;button type="submit"&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;<br>
&lt;/form&gt;

</div>

</li>

<li>
<strong>Secure Data Transmission Improvements :</strong>

<ul>
<li>Use the POST method.</li>
<li>Enable HTTPS.</li>
<li>Validate user input.</li>
<li>Encrypt sensitive information.</li>
<li>Implement secure authentication mechanisms.</li>
</ul>

</li>

</ol>

